Drop the vendor RAID CLIs here before running ./build.sh
=======================================================

The three binaries are distributed by the vendors and CANNOT be shipped inside
this repository. Put the decompressed ELF binaries straight into this directory
(no wrapper scripts, no directory named like the tool):

    config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/storcli     LSI / Broadcom MegaRAID
    config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/arcconf     PMC / Microsemi Adaptec
    config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/ssacli      HPE Smart Array

Where they come from:

  storcli   Broadcom (or your OEM's support page) -> "storcli - MR7.x" ->
            unix/StorCLI_rel.zip  ->  unzip  ->  storcli*_ARM.zip? no:
            take   storcli_all_os/Linux/storcli？ Standard layout after unzip:
                    versionChangeSet/univ_viva_cli_rel/storcli_all_os/Linux/storcli
            Rename it to `storcli`, chmod 755, drop it here.

  arcconf   Microsemi / Adaptec -> "ARCCONF Command Line Utility" ->
            arcconf_v3.*_linux_x64.tar.gz or the zip that contains the
            cmdline/arcconf binary. Rename to `arcconf`, chmod 755.

  ssacli    HPE Support Center -> "Smart Storage Administrator CLI" ->
            ssacli-*.x86_64.rpm works too:
                rpm2cpio ssacli-*.rpm | cpio -idmv
                cp usr/sbin/ssacli .../config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/
            or use the .deb variant with dpkg-deb -x.

Verification before building:

    for t in storcli arcconf ssacli; do
        [ -x "config/includes.chroot/usr/local/bin/$t" ] && echo "$t ok"
    done

Notes:

* Only the tools actually present are used; detection priority is
  storcli -> arcconf -> ssacli -> sg3_utils.
* With no vendor tool present the image still works in "generic" mode using
  sg3_utils + smartctl + hdparm + nvme-cli, but it can only reach disks that are
  directly visible to the OS (no disks behind a hardware RAID).
* Keep the binary name exactly as shown - `core/detect.py` resolves them through
  PATH and expects those names.
